  "report": "CHANGES_REQUESTED: one documented creator boundary breach remains; no other Standards breach or baseline smell was found in this exact37-file delta. B-GATE-RETENTION-STANDARDS-01: race/freeze.py hashes the fresh archive with unbounded Path.read_bytes(); verdict/freeze.py similarly reads the archive and suite indices by pathname. Earlier stat/scan guards do not bound a growing or replaced input at the actual read. Reuse no-follow, nonblocking regular-FD reads with fstat and cumulative caps; retain the actual original writer bytes separately.\n\nAfter confirmed custody-window closure, independent stdlib streaming hashed all133177 race members and64 outer members, including133241 regular payloads, complete tar headers and inventories. Race's98710 artifact references,1056 source files against Git7931, all eight verifier receipts, four numeric0/0/1/1 receipts, source/plan/helper/observer/build/review chains and cross-capsule equality were checked. Ordinary uses its previously complete independent proof and unchanged pin, without repeating its1.3GB scan.\n\nBoth native suites preserve12445 PASS/6 FAIL/0 NOT_RUN,868 real PIDIFF PASS and29 pressure-named PASS, of which15 meet the fixed regex. Full stdout, original STARTING intent, completed false JSON/Markdown verdict, refused assembly, unchanged matrix and zero imported rows remain honest. Recorded public verification and eight private-copy refusals per new consumer were read, not executed.\n\nThe actual source is7931; later ticket17/2306 source has no current qualification from this history. No Go binary, observer, controller, verifier, test, credential or network operation was executed, and no repository/raw byte was changed.",
